{
  "about": "Files moved here byte for byte from the engine (Trillion-X/trillion-rust src and crates) at 5fbc2ff4b1bf16622e2472f0638db9f79da980e9 on the owners order (Nov 15 2026): anything that is not one of the five core jobs is a tool and leaves the engine, so the old workspace pages, the app pages, the tool fact page, the tool label words, the tool-run page routes, the native entry page and the collation crate live in the Workshop. Each names its source path and commit and the identity of its bytes there and here; the one file whose bytes here differ names the call that swapped a real persons name in a comment for a made-up one. Lane engine-core-stands (trillion-rust 4643917907, Nov 15 2026) added the rest of the workspace files and their tests; each entry names its own commit.",
  "source": "Trillion-X/trillion-rust",
  "package": "trillion-workshop",
  "calls": [
    {
      "id": "owner-name-in-comment",
      "find": "\\b(?:J[i]bran|B[r]ian)\\b",
      "replace": "the owner",
      "means": "A real persons name in a source comment, swapped for a made-up one: a public tree holds made-up data only."
    },
    {
      "id": "example-email-shape-in-a-host-test",
      "find": "@(?:service\\.example|mcp\\.example\\.test|app\\.example|other\\.example\\.test)(?=\")",
      "replace": "@example.com",
      "means": "An address with user information on a made-up host reads as a real email address to the public push check; the same refusal on the example.com host keeps the test's meaning (user information is refused)."
    }
  ],
